.TH rl 1 "2026-05-20" "Relier 0.1.0" "rl(1)"
.SH NAME
rl \- Relier command-line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rl
.RI [ options ] " <group> <command> " [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rl
is the command-line interface for
.B Relier ,
the reliability layer for Celery (built for FastAPI; supports
Flask, Django, and any other Python web framework or script). It provides
subcommands for task monitoring, Dead Letter Queue management, worker
operations, chaos engineering, SLO tracking, and cluster administration.
.PP
Every
.B rl
command is a short-lived process that talks directly to the same Redis your
workers use \- there is no daemon, no API server, no extra infrastructure to
deploy. If Redis is reachable, the CLI works.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the CLI version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the top-level help message.
.SH TOP-LEVEL COMMANDS
.TP
.B rl man [\-\-plain]
Print this manual, rendered with Rich Markdown by default. Pass
.B \-\-plain
to get raw Markdown for piping into another tool.
.TP
.B rl doctor
Check Redis and cluster dependency health. Exits non-zero if Redis is
unreachable. Suitable as a Docker / Kubernetes liveness probe.
.TP
.B rl bench [\-\-iterations N]
Measure Relier dispatch overhead vs raw Celery
.BR .delay() .
Uses the always-loaded
.B chaos_noop
target so it runs in any environment.
.TP
.B rl run-resurrector [\-\-loglevel LEVEL] [\-\-interval SECS]
Start the Phoenix resurrector engine. Monitors the cluster for dead workers
and re-queues orphaned tasks. Typically runs as a dedicated 'guardian'
process or container.
.B rl resurrect
is a hidden alias retained for backwards compatibility.
.SH CLUSTER COMMANDS
.B rl cluster
manages the bundled Docker Compose stack (workers, resurrector, Redis,
OpenTelemetry collector, Prometheus, Grafana).
.TP
.B rl cluster up [\-d|\-\-detach|\-\-no\-detach]
Start the full Relier stack via Docker Compose (default: detached).
.TP
.B rl cluster down
Gracefully shut down the Relier stack.
.TP
.B rl cluster status
Check Docker Compose stack and Redis connectivity.
.TP
.B rl cluster scale N
Scale the worker pool to N replicas.
.TP
.B rl cluster logs [\-f|\-\-follow] [service]
Tail stack logs. Optionally filter to a single service (e.g.
.IR worker ,
.IR redis ,
.IR resurrector ).
.SH TASK COMMANDS
.TP
.B rl tasks inflight [\-f|\-\-follow] [\-\-worker ID]
Show all tasks currently executing across the cluster.
.B \-\-follow
refreshes the view every 2 seconds.
.B \-\-worker
restricts output to a single worker.
.TP
.B rl tasks list
One-shot inflight task table.
.TP
.B rl tasks top
A top-like summary: active workers, queue depth, and p95 latency.
.TP
.B rl tasks inspect task_id
Show the full payload, execution state, and Phoenix metadata for a task.
.TP
.B rl tasks retry task_id
Re-queue a failed or quarantined task. Checks the DLQ first; falls back to
the Phoenix payload for orphaned tasks. Preserves the resurrection count.
.TP
.B rl tasks cancel task_id [\-\-no\-terminate]
Revoke and cancel a task. Sends SIGTERM to the running process by default.
Pass
.B \-\-no\-terminate
to mark the task revoked without killing a running process.
.TP
.B rl tasks logs task_id [\-f|\-\-follow]
Display state transitions and metadata for a task.
.B \-\-follow
polls Redis every 2 seconds until the task exits.
.SH WORKER COMMANDS
.TP
.B rl worker status
List all active workers with per-worker session metrics.
.TP
.B rl worker drain worker_id
Initiate a graceful shutdown for a worker: it stops accepting new tasks and
finishes (or hands off) current work before exiting.
.TP
.B rl worker restart worker_id
Send a shutdown signal to a worker for a rolling restart. The process manager
(Docker, systemd, Kubernetes) restarts the worker automatically.
.TP
.B rl worker reset worker_id
Clear per-session success/failed counters for a worker.
.SH DLQ COMMANDS
The Dead Letter Queue holds tasks that cannot be safely retried.
.TP
.B rl dlq list
List all quarantined tasks in the DLQ.
.TP
.B rl dlq inspect task_id
Show the full payload, error context, and resurrection history for a
quarantined task.
.TP
.B rl dlq release task_id
Un-quarantine a task and re-submit it to its original queue. Preserves the
resurrection count.
.TP
.B rl dlq retry-all
Re-submit every task in the DLQ.
.TP
.B rl dlq purge \-\-confirm
Permanently delete every DLQ entry. Requires
.B \-\-confirm
to proceed (irreversible).
.SH SLO COMMANDS
.TP
.B rl slo status [\-\-target FRACTION]
Show current error-budget burn rates across the 1h, 6h, and 3d windows.
.B \-\-target
overrides the default 99.9% SLO target.
.TP
.B rl slo report [\-\-period 1h|6h|3d] [\-\-format table|json]
Historical burn-rate report. JSON output is suitable for dashboards.
.SH CHAOS COMMANDS
Run these only against a non-production cluster.
.TP
.B rl chaos worker-kill [\-\-worker ID] [\-\-seed] [\-\-seed-duration SECS] [\-\-watch] [\-\-watch-duration SECS]
Send SIGKILL to a worker process.
.B \-\-seed
dispatches a long-running task first so Phoenix has something to resurrect.
.B \-\-watch
streams resurrection events to the console after the kill.
.TP
.B rl chaos network-partition [\-\-secs N]
Simulate a Redis network partition for N seconds.
.TP
.B rl chaos load-spike [\-\-rps N] [\-\-duration SECS]
Flood the dispatch path with N requests per second to stress admission
control.
.TP
.B rl chaos task-corrupt
Inject a malformed poison-pill envelope into the task queue. Expect a DLQ
quarantine with
.IR PayloadIntegrityError .
.TP
.B rl chaos slow-task [\-\-duration SECS]
Dispatch a task that sleeps longer than its configured hard_timeout,
triggering the timeout pipeline and DLQ quarantine.
.SH CONFIG COMMANDS
.TP
.B rl config show
Print all active configuration values. Passwords and connection URLs are
redacted.
.TP
.B rl config validate
Validate Redis policy (\fImaxmemory-policy=noeviction\fR) and all
.B RELIER_*
environment variables against the settings schema.
.TP
.B rl config set KEY VALUE
Write a configuration key/value pair to the local
.I .env
file. Restart affected workers for the change to take effect.
.SH ADMISSION COMMANDS
.TP
.B rl admission status
Show the current admission control state, request count, and load-shedding
percentage.
.SH ADMIN COMMANDS
Low-level Redis maintenance. Use with care.
.TP
.B rl admin config
Display the active cluster configuration (abbreviated).
.TP
.B rl admin purge-locks
Force-delete every idempotency lock sentinel from Redis.
.TP
.B rl admin reset-admission
Reset admission control counters across the cluster.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Live task monitoring:
.PP
.nf
rl tasks inflight --follow
rl tasks inflight --follow --worker rl-worker-2
.fi
.PP
Inspect and release a quarantined task:
.PP
.nf
rl dlq list
rl dlq inspect 5df7f30a-8404-41e1-bb80-6d480771f13f
rl dlq release 5df7f30a-8404-41e1-bb80-6d480771f13f
.fi
.PP
Validate Phoenix resurrection end-to-end:
.PP
.nf
rl chaos worker-kill --seed --watch --watch-duration 60
.fi
.PP
Export SLO data for a dashboard:
.PP
.nf
rl slo report --format json | jq .
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
.PP
This man page is shipped in the source tree at
.IR man/rl.1 .
The same content is bundled into the package and rendered cross-platform by
.B rl man ,
so installing the man page is optional. To install it on Linux for
.BR man (1)
use:
.PP
.nf
sudo cp man/rl.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
sudo mandb
man rl
.fi
.PP
On macOS:
.PP
.nf
sudo cp man/rl.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
man rl
.fi
.PP
On Windows, there is no
.BR man (1)
command;
.B rl man
is the supported entry point.
